mask on  yeah dramatic video shows  lawmakers and staff inside the house  chambers rioters stormed the building  yesterday afternoon  now some lawmakers were trapped on the  second floor that's known as the house  gallery  after representatives on the first floor  were evacuated  you can actually hear what sounds like  gunshots and see lawmakers hiding behind  the gallery railing  as some of them even put on emergency  masks now we have an image that shows  representative take a look at this this  is jason crowe from colorado  and representative susan wilde oh my  goodness of pennsylvania crouching down  together  they join us now to talk about that i'm  so glad that the two of you are okay i  listen guys i thought it was  traumatizing just seeing the picture  sitting in the safety of my home at from  my kitchen table  i can't imagine what it was like for the  two of you jason if you would start us  off please  congressman crowe what exactly is  happening in this moment  well this is the moment where we got  trapped in the house chamber they had  evacuated leadership  as soon as the outer court on the  security barrier had been broken at the  capitol  and they evacuated the members who were  on the house floor and then they started  to evacuate us but by that point  uh the uh mob the rioters had broken in  and had surrounded the chamber so they  uh closed the doors and we had to lock  the doors and started to barricade them  to prevent  uh the mob from getting in and they were  they were trying to ram down the doors  and we were  at that point thinking we might have to  fight our way out you're clearly  comforting your colleague there at that  moment why did you think that was  necessary  my heart goes out to you susan while  because i could see the concern on your  face jason what were you thinking as you  looked at her  well i mean susan is my friend and um  you know i was uh  upset about the situation she was upset  about it and  i did what i think any friend would want  to do and i just  let her know that i was there for her  and that we would get through it  yeah susan what was going through your  mind at that moment did you think your  life was in danger at that particular  time  i i think i did believe that there was  chaos and confusion i had never been in  a situation like that unlike my  colleague here who's been in combat  situations i had  not it was terribly concerning that  photograph was actually  first sent to me by my adult son  who texted it to me later in the day  needless to say that's not  what you want your children to see you  facetimed your children during this  didn't you what did you say to them what  did you say  i actually that's my daughter yeah that  you're showing on the screen  her name and um yes i asked my children  to call me and  we facetimed very briefly i didn't know  what was going to happen next  and i wanted to make sure that i had  some communication with them  it was the the last thing in the world i  wanted to do i was afraid that  it would just terrorize them but at the  same time if the worst happened i didn't  want them to not  have heard from me as a child to see  your parents in that situation i know  that was very upsetting we understand  that you all were taken  to a secure location can you say now  where that was  how many people were in the room and  what did you all talk about at that  moment  well we were taken to the ways and means  committee room which is probably the  largest committee room um it's over in  longworth  and i would say at its peak there were  about  somewhere close to 400 people in there  mostly members but some staff  it wasn't nearly big enough as a room  considering the current pandemic  and social distancing issues and so  forth there were an awful lot of  unmasked members republicans who were  specifically asked  to put their masks on that just added  another layer of stress to a very very  stressful day did you talk about how you  were going to proceed  after all of this ended  well i think we're still processing what  exactly happened and i think um  you know as i i have about three hours  of sleep under my belt right now i think  susan has about the same  uh but as i've reflected more on it um  frankly i'm pretty angry right now  i'm angry about the traitors who  stormed the capitol you called this a  coup on twitter  yeah that that was their intent to stop  the transition of power i don't know  what else to call it  that's what was happening they delayed  it but they did not stop it because our  democracy and our government  is stronger than these uh these  treasonous  uh traitors uh but they need to be  brought to justice and they need to be  brought to justice fast  are you angry at the president too  congressman crow  many believe he incited this can you  talk about that  well there's it's not it's not a  question of whether or not uh they  believe he incited that this isn't a  question of the tooth fairy or or santa  claus  uh he did incite this directly these are  his words  he did it he is a violent man he's an  ill man  but this is not a story about donald  trump anymore because we have known for  many many years  who he is there should come as no  surprise  this is really a story of the enablers  the members of congress  the inner circle the members who have  allowed us to get to this point  were you are you concerned that that  this happened  i mean that this was allowed to happen  in the first place how did you feel  that capitol police responded and how do  you feel the city  police responded you know that's  that's something that still remains to  be determined  we were inside the building the entire  day so we didn't have the opportunity to  see what was happening but we have since  seen video  and clips and it's very concerning  um as i said to jason just before we  came on the show  it's not just about the safety of  members of congress but in the average  day when we're not in  a pandemic thousands of members of the  public  are scattered throughout the capital the  idea  that that building can be stormed so  easily  and that security can be overcome and  and literally  take over the capitol for an extended  period of time this wasn't just a brief  thing you've seen the pictures of these  people  scattered throughout the building taking  pictures of themselves  with you know so very very concerning  for  for all of us yeah thank you for the  reminder that we're in the middle of a  pandemic  yeah people need to know listen we're  still living in very dangerous times  representatives jason crowe and susan  wilde thank you both  for joining us this morning and we are  glad you are okay  thank you so much and

